msgid ""
"Which generates the following bytecode (this can be produced via `interp::"
"Function::dump()`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConstantInterpreter.md:287
msgid ""
"As you can see, all instructions here are type-aware. We're first pushing "
"both parameter values to the stack. Then the `Add` opcode will add them up "
"and push the result to the stack, which will be returned via the `Ret` "
"opcode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConstantInterpreter.md:291
msgid "Debugging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConstantInterpreter.md:293
msgid "Here are a few hints when working on the bytecode interpreter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConstantInterpreter.md:295
msgid ""
"Setting a breakpoint on `CCEDiag` and `FFDiag` will stop the debugger when a "
"diagnostic is emitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConstantInterpreter.md:297
msgid ""
"If you want to see the bytecode of a function call `dump()` on the `interp::"
"Function`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConstantInterpreter.md:298
msgid ""
"Additionally to the last point, `interp::Function::dump(CodePtr)` exists, "
"which you can pass the current `OpPC` and it will then show you where in the "
"bytecode that opcode is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConstantInterpreter.md:300
msgid ""
"`interp::Pointer` has an `operator<<` that prints useful information. Try it "
"e.g. via `llvm::errs() << Ptr << '\\n';`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConstantInterpreter.md:302
msgid "Printing `APValue` instances also works via `APValue::dump()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ConstantInterpreter.md:303
msgid ""
"If you want to see *everything* that's being evaluated, add debugging output "
"to the `evaluate*` functions in `Context.cpp`."
msgstr ""
